--------------------------- Changelog -----------------------------

1.0.c - UNRELEASED
Fixed - A camp fleet that loses a fight to you gives up the rupture and leaves, instead of holding it until destroyed
Fixed - Job intel names the market and star system to deliver to, and switches to "Return to" once you have the catch; a cleared camp job points back to the fisher once the proof is aboard
Added - Neutrino Lens module for the Lens Array. Shows rare, epic and legendary patterns as rarity-coloured Neutrino Detector spikes. Grants the detector if missing.
Changed - Recovered treasure now has aligned quantities; range data displays as "Range data: <fish>".
Changed - Contract hunters respond less often to single harpoon hits, but may pursue unpaid repair bills or fleeing after identification following a dark hit. Paying the fine calls them off.
Changed - Crews with unpaid repair bills now report you to local patrols instead of chasing you. All patrols in the system demand payment on sight until the fine is paid.
Added - Crablobab sells Party Horn after acquiring Celebration Charges, followed by Crab Fanfare. Both replace the catch sound and can be previewed before purchase and selected in the Outfitter.
Removed - Failed Quorum catches no longer spawn 12 extra decoys.
Fixed - Needle Sensor ripples are larger, brighter and visible at greater zoom distances.
Fixed - Dormant epics and legendaries now leave trails under breach lights.
Added - Uncommon fishing chests have a 25% chance to contain unknown range data alongside normal loot, including with the Lifting Rig.
Fixed - Loading saves with Lantern Jack surfaced in the current system no longer crashes.
Fixed - Reduced performance cost of epic and legendary trails under breach lights.
Fixed - Automatic job and Outfitter payments no longer consume legendary fish.
Removed - Disabled legendary tribute at Kanta's Den pending dialogue replacement.
Fixed - Corrected aquarium swimming orientation for 13 species, including Dopefish and several legendaries.
Adjusted - Harpoons hitting shields no longer play the catch sound.
Fixed - Legendary floating text use shield or mote colour instead of a generic UI highlight
Added - Lantern Jack now coils for 0.3 seconds within 300 units of a mote, then dashes through it to feed (also: added vfx)

1.0.b

General
Added - Temporary industry image

Fisherman
Fixed - Nearby settlements no longer prevent the Fisherman from approaching you for the tutorial
Fixed - Finishing the Fisherman's "Why a fish?" questions no longer shows an empty Continue before "You could have told me this before I started."
Fixed - Fisherman tutorial lessons no longer send you to systems with a neutron star
Adjusted - The Fisherman's first lesson now points at the rupture closest to him
Added - Selling fish to the Fisherman can unpack crates again after using "Pack into crates"
Fixed - Hovering the "Pack into crates" button in the Fisherman sale screen no longer repeats the click sound
Fixed - Undo in the Fisherman's range data shop takes back every purchase in sequence, newest first, like the Outfitter
Adjusted - Buncha dialogue
Fixed - "Set autopilot" on tutorial and chart request intel now targets a visiting Fisherman in your current system instead of a boat elsewhere

Fish
Added - New portraits for 16 fish that had placeholders until now
Added - Dopefish, a rare Epic catch that barely moves and is very easy to land
Fixed - System fish counts no longer include a species that never spawns there, which made a full system show 16 species
Fixed - A star system never offers more than 15 species; a legendary in a full system temporarily takes one of those slots

Legendaries
Added - Lantern Jack's lure call now plays a distress-call sound
Added - Harpoons deflected by a legendary's shield play a varied shield-hit sound
Added - Epic fish leave a fainter purple version of the legendary trail under breach lights
Adjusted - Buried and diving legendaries and epics no longer leave a trail
Added - A foghorn sounds when a legendary haunt starts and ends

Outfitter
Added - Hovering an Outfitter fish count shows the species of that rarity aboard

Cargo and items
Fixed - Fish, crate and pile tooltips only show their right-click hints for fish in your fleet's cargo, not in markets, storage or selection screens
Adjusted - Fish art on crate labels in cargo is drawn sharper
Adjusted - Tooltips across most items
Fixed - Fish, crates and piles sold to a market now disappear when its stock refreshes

Codex
Added - Codex pages of caught fish show a size distribution chart with your best and latest catch

1.0.a
Added - Initial Mod Release

General
Adjusted - Release downloads leave out development tools, libraries and source files
Adjusted - Rewrote fishing settings descriptions to explain their effects and limits more clearly

Development
Added - Changelog and release instructions
